{"version":1,"slug":"Others__Quantitative_Aptitude_-_SSC_Super_Practice_35_(20Q)","path":"Others/Quantitative Aptitude - SSC Super Practice 35 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"Quantitative Aptitude - SSC Super Practice 35 (20Q).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>LCM of two number is 56 times their HCF, with the sum of their HCF and LCM being 1710. If one of the two numbers is 240, then what is the other number?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) &#2325;&#2366; 56 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; HCF &#2324;&#2352; LCM &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; 1710 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 240 &#2361;&#2376;,&#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">57</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">57</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">171</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">171</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1680</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1680</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">210</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">210</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let HCF and LCM of two numbers be H and L respectively.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>L = 56H ........ (1)</p><p>L + H = 1710 ....... (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>56H + H = 1710</p><p>H = 30</p><p>L = 1680</p><p>We know that:</p><p>Product of two numbers = Product of their HCF and LCM</p><p>240 * N = 1680 * 30</p><p>N = 210</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the LCM of 3.6, 1.8 and 0.144?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>3.6, 1.8 &#2324;&#2352; 0.144 &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3.6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3.6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3600</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">360</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">360</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20002/image071.png\"></p><p><img width=52 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20002/image072.png\"></p><p><img width=85 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20002/image073.png\"></p><p>LCM of 3.6, 1.8, and 0.144 = <img width=171 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20002/image074.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Two numbers are in the ratio 9 : 7. If their HCF is 6, find their LCM.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 9:7 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 6 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">189</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">189</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">126</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">126</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">378</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">378</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">252</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">252</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the numbers are 9x and 7x respectively. </p><p>HCF of 9x and 7x = x = 6</p><p>LCM of 9x and 7x = 63x = 63  X  6</p><p>= 378</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The HCF of two numbers is one-twentieth of their LCM. If one of the numbers is 96 and the difference of the LCM and the HCF is 456, then what is the other number? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; LCM &#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2368;&#2360;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 96 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; LCM &#2324;&#2352; HCF &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 456 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? </p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">48</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">120</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">120</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">144</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">144</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">72</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let other number = x</p><p>Let LCM = y</p><p>HCF = y/20</p><p>=&gt; LCM  -  HCF = 456</p><p>y  -  y/20 = 456</p><p>y = 480</p><p>LCM = 480</p><p>HCF = 480/20 = 24</p><p>Product of two numbers = LCM * HCF</p><p>96 * x = 480 * 24</p><p>x = 120</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p><div>&nbsp;The HCF of <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'> 1</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>2 </span></div>, <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'> 3</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>4 </span></div>, <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'> 5</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>6 </span></div>, and <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'> 7</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>8 </span></div> is&#58;&nbsp;</div></p><p></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p><div><div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'> 1</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>2 </span></div>, <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'> 3</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>4 </span></div>, <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'> 5</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>6 </span></div>, and <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'> 7</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;'>_________</span><span style='display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center'>8 </span></div> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) &#2361;&#2376;:</div></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">105/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">105/2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7/24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7/24</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1/48</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/48</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>HCF of fractions = HCF of numerator/LCM of denominator</p><p>HCF of 1/2, 3/4, 5/6, and 7/8 = HCF of 1, 3, 5, and 7/LCM of 2, 4, 6, and 8</p><p>HCF of 1, 3, 5, and 7 = 1</p><p>LCM of 2, 4, 6, and 8 = 24</p><p>Required HCF = 1/24</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The product of two numbers is 38025 and their Highest Common Factor is 65. What is the Least Common Multiple of these numbers?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; 38025 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; 65 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">455</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">455</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">585</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">585</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">715</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">715</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">435</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">435</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Since the HCF of two numbers is 65, then let the numbers are 65a and 65b respectively. ['a' and 'b' are co-prime.]</p><p>Product of two numbers = 65a  X  65b = 38025</p><p>ab = 9</p><p>LCM of two numbers = 65ab = 65  X  9</p><p>= 585</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the highest common factor (HCF) of x and y is 15, then the HCF of 36x<sup>2</sup> -  81y<sup>2</sup> and 81x<sup>2</sup> -  9y<sup>2</sup> is divisible by.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x &#2324;&#2352; y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 15 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 36x<sup>2</sup> - 81y<sup>2</sup> &#2324;&#2352; 81x<sup>2</sup> - 9y<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2366; HCF _____ &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">135</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">135</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">120</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">120</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">180</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">180</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">90</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">90</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>36x<sup>2</sup> -  81y<sup>2</sup> = 9[(2x)<sup>2</sup> - (3y)<sup>2</sup>] = 9*(2x+3y)*(2x-3y)</p><p>81x<sup>2</sup> -  9y<sup>2</sup>= 9[(3x)<sup>2</sup> - y<sup>2</sup>] = 9*(3x+y)*(3x-y)</p><p>HCF of x and y is 15.</p><p>HCF of 36x<sup>2</sup> -  81y<sup>2</sup> and 81x<sup>2</sup> -  9y<sup>2</sup>= 9*15*15</p><p>HCF of 36x<sup>2</sup> -  81y<sup>2</sup> and 81x<sup>2</sup> -  9y<sup>2</sup> is divisible by 135.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the greatest number that will divide 49, 147 and 322 to leave the same remainder in each case.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; 49, 147 &#2324;&#2352; 322 &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><b>We know that:</b> If two or more numbers give the same remainder when divided by some other number, then their difference must give a remainder of zero when divided by that number.</p><p>So,</p><p>Greatest number that will divide 49, 147 and 322 to leave the same remainder in each case = HCF of (147  -  49), (322  -  49), and (322  -  147)</p><p>= HCF of 98, 273, and 175</p><p>98 = 2 * 7<sup>2</sup></p><p>273 = 3 * 7 * 13</p><p>175 = 5<sup>2</sup> * 7</p><p>HCF of 98, 273, and 175 = 7</p><p>Hence, required number = 7</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The product of the two numbers is 1500 and their HCF is 10. The number of such possible pairs is/are:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; 1500 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 10 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2320;&#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;/&#2361;&#2376;&#2306; :</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Product of the two numbers = 1500</p><p>Highest common factor is 10.</p><p>Let numbers be 10x and 10y.</p><p>So, 10x * 10y = 1500</p><p>=&gt; x * y = 15</p><p>The possible pairs of x and y are (1, 15), (5, 3) .</p><p>So, (10, 150), (50, 30) are the two possible pairs.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The largest number that can divide 147, 183 and 271 leaving remainders 11, 13 and 16, respectively, is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2379; 147, 183 &#2324;&#2352; 271 &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 11, 13 &#2324;&#2352; 16 &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">17</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>147 - 11 = 136</p><p>183 - 13 = 170</p><p>271 - 16 = 255</p><p>Find GCD of 136, 170, 255</p><p>Factorize: 136 = 2<sup>3</sup> * 17, 170 = 2 * 5 * 17, 255 = 3 * 5 * 17</p><p>GCD = <b>17</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>An oil dealer had three types of oil. 403 litres of the first kind, 434 litres of the second kind and 465 litres of the third kind. Find the maximum volume of oil, filled in each barrel, if equal number of barrels are filled.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2375;&#2354; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2375;&#2354; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; 403 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; 434 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; 465 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2376;&#2352;&#2354; &#2349;&#2352;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2348;&#2376;&#2352;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2340;&#2375;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">52 litres</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">52 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">48 litres</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">31 litres</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">31 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">41 litres</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">41 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>For equal number of barrels, we have to calculate the HCF of all three types of oil.</p><p>HCF of 403, 434, 465 = 31</p><p>Maximum volume of oil, filled in each barrel = 31 litres</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The least number of square tiles required to pave the ceiling of a room 525 centimetre long and 378 centimetre broad is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>525 &#2360;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 378 &#2360;&#2375;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2340; &#2348;&#2367;&#2331;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">178</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">178</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">150</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">150</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">380</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">380</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">450</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">450</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>To minimize the number of square tiles, use the largest possible tile size, which is the GCD of 525 cm and 378 cm.</p><p>GCD = 21</p><p>Tile side = 21 cm.</p><p>Tiles along length = 525 / 21 = 25</p><p>Tiles along breadth = 378 / 21 = 18</p><p>Total tiles = 25 * 18 = 450</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Three red lights on the same road start blinking at the same time and blink repeatedly after every 4, 6 and 8 minutes, respectively. How many times will they blink together in an interval of 3 hours, excluding blinking together at the starting moment?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2350;&#2325;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2361;&#2352; 4, 6 &#2324;&#2352; 8 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;-&#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2330;&#2350;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340;&#2368; &#2346;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2330;&#2350;&#2325;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352;, 3 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2330;&#2350;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>LCM of 4, 6, 8 = 24 minutes</p><p>Interval = 3 hours = 180 minutes</p><p>Number of times when the lights blink together = 180/24 = 7.5 =&gt; 7 times</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The largest three-digit number that gives the same remainder 2 when divided by 3, 5 and 9 is ________.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>3, 5 &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; 2 &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; ________ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">999</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">999</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">984</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">984</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">998</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">998</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">992</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">992</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>LCM of 3, 5 and 9 = 45</p><p>Largest three-digit number = 999</p><p>999 = 22*45 + 9</p><p>So, 990 is divisible by 3, 5 and 9.</p><p>Hence, the number = 990 + 2 = 992</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A and B are two prime numbers such that A &gt; B and their LCM is 209. The value of B<sup>2 </sup> -  A is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; A&gt; B &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) 209 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; B<sup>2 </sup>- A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">111</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">111</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">102</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">102</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">121</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">121</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">109</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">109</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Since A and B are two prime numbers which means their HCF will be 1.</p><p>Hence, product of two prime numbers will be equal to LCM.</p><p>A * B = 209</p><p>A * B = 19 * 11</p><p>After comparing:</p><p>A = 19</p><p>B = 11</p><p>Now,</p><p>B<sup>2</sup>  -  A</p><p>= 11<sup>2</sup>  -  19</p><p>= 102</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The LCM of 2<sup>3</sup>  X  9<sup>2</sup>  X  13, 2<sup>2</sup>  X  13<sup>2</sup>  X  19 and 9<sup>3</sup>  X  13<sup>2</sup>  X  19<sup>2</sup> is - </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>2<sup>3</sup> X 9<sup>2</sup> X 13, 2<sup>2</sup> X 13<sup>2</sup> X 19 &#2324;&#2352; 9<sup>3</sup> X 13<sup>2</sup> X 19<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2366; LCM &#2361;&#2376; - </p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2<sup>3</sup> X 9<sup>2</sup> X 13<sup>2</sup> X 19</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2<sup>3</sup> X 9<sup>2</sup> X 13<sup>2</sup> X 19</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2<sup>3</sup> X 9<sup>3</sup> X 13<sup>2</sup> X 19<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2<sup>3</sup> X 9<sup>3</sup> X 13<sup>2</sup> X 19<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2<sup>2</sup> X 9<sup>2</sup> X 13<sup>2</sup> X 19<sup>3</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2<sup>2</sup> X 9<sup>2</sup> X 13<sup>2</sup> X 19<sup>3</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2<sup>2</sup> X 9<sup>3</sup> X 13 X 19<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2<sup>2</sup> X 9<sup>3</sup> X 13 X 19<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>For LCM, we take maximum power of each number.</p><p>LCM of 2<sup>3</sup>  X  9<sup>2</sup>  X  13, 2<sup>2</sup>  X  13<sup>2</sup>  X  19 and 9<sup>3</sup>  X  13<sup>2</sup>  X  19<sup>2</sup> = 2<sup>3</sup>  X  9<sup>3</sup>  X  13<sup>2</sup>  X  19<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A milk vendor has 75 litres of cow milk, 45 litres of toned milk and 30 litres of full cream milk. These should be placed in different trays such that each tray contains the same quantity of milk and two kinds of milk should not be mixed in a tray. What is the least number of trays required to place all the milk?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; 75 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2327;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343;, 45 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2335;&#2379;&#2306;&#2337; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2324;&#2352; 30 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2347;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2350; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2352;&#2326;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2379; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2344; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2352;&#2326;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>HCF of 75, 45, 30 = 15</p><p>Trays:</p><p>Cow: 75 / 15 = 5</p><p>Toned: 45 / 15 = 3</p><p>Full cream: 30 / 15 = 2</p><p>Total = 5 + 3 + 2 = 10</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The LCM of x<sup>2</sup> &#8722; 8x + 15 and x<sup>2</sup> &#8722; 5x + 6 is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>x<sup>2</sup> &#8722; 8x + 15 &#2324;&#2352; x<sup>2</sup> &#8722; 5x + 6 &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">(x - 2) (x - 3) (x &#8722; 5)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(x - 2) (x - 3) (x &#8722; 5)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(x &#8722; 6)<sup>2</sup> (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(x &#8722; 6)<sup>2</sup> (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(x &#8722; 6) (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(x &#8722; 6) (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(x + 6) (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(x + 6) (x + 1) (x &#8722; 3)</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Factors of x<sup>2</sup> - 8x+15 = (x-3) (x-5)</p><p>Factors of x<sup>2</sup>&#8722;5x+6 = (x-3) (x-2)</p><p>LCM = (x-2) (x-3) (x-5)</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The sum of the two numbers is 45. Their HCF and LCM are 5 and 70 respectively. Find the sum of the reciprocal of the two numbers.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 45 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5 &#2324;&#2352; 70 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">9/70</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9/70</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3/140</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3/140</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4/35</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4/35</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3/16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3/16</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Since the HCF of two numbers is 5, the let the numbers are 5a and 5b respectively. ['a' and 'b' are co-prime numbers and a &gt; b.]</p><p>LCM of 5a and 5b = 5ab = 70</p><p>ab = 14 ...... (1)</p><p>Sum of two numbers = 5a + 5b = 45</p><p>a + b = 9 ....... (2)</p><p>From (1) and (2):</p><p>(a + b)/ab = 9/14</p><p>a/ab + b/ab = 9/14</p><p>1/b + 1/a = 9/14</p><p>Sum of reciprocal of the two numbers = 1/5a + 1/5b = 9/(5 * 14)</p><p>= 9/70</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the smallest integer that is multiple of 5, 8 and 15?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367; 5, 8 &#2324;&#2352; 15 &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">60</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">600</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">600</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">120</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">120</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Required answer = LCM of 5, 8, and 15 = 120</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}